.TH "CAPNG_UPDATE_LIST" "3" "November 2026" "Red Hat" "Libcap-ng API"
.SH NAME
capng_update_list \- update the stored capabilities settings from a counted list
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B #include <cap-ng.h>
.sp
int capng_update_list(capng_act_t action, capng_type_t type,
.br
                      const unsigned int *capabilities, size_t count);

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

capng_update_list adds or drops each of the
.I count
capabilities in the
.I capabilities
array, in the sets selected by
.IR type .
The
.I action
and
.I type
arguments are the same as for
.BR capng_update (3).
Each element must be a capability number no greater than
.BR capng_last_cap (3).

Unlike
.BR capng_updatev (3),
the length of the list is explicit, so no terminating value is read, and
every element is checked before any change is made. If any element is
invalid, no capability is updated and the internal state is left unchanged.
A
.I count
of zero is a successful no-op, and
.I capabilities
may then be NULL.

This only changes libcap-ng's internal state. Use
.BR capng_apply (3)
to transfer the result to the kernel.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

This returns 0 on success and -1 on failure. On failure,
.I errno
is set to
.B EINVAL
when the list is invalid.

.SH "SEE ALSO"

.BR capng_update (3),
.BR capng_updatev (3),
.BR capng_last_cap (3),
.BR capng_apply (3),
.BR capabilities (7)

.SH AUTHOR
Steve Grubb
